History Views – Frontend Scope & Requirements
App Scope

You are building two read-only views with minimal interaction:

Daily Summary View

Individual Shift Summary View

Each view will contain:

One pie chart

One data table

Pie Chart
Data (provided by backend)

machine_uptime

available_downtime

unavailable_downtime

The chart should show relative proportions only.
Total time may be displayed separately (e.g., above the chart).

Requirements

Legend required (clear color → metric mapping)

Tooltip on hover showing value + percentage

Colors should be clean, readable, and consistent across views

Frontend may compute percentages only for visualization.

Data Table
Metrics (all values come from backend)

Planned runtime

Total runtime

Machine uptime

Available downtime

Unavailable downtime

Total stops

Machine error stops

Total parts

OEE

No calculations or derivations should be done on the frontend.

Architecture Overview

All analytics data will be provided to the frontend via an API that is polled at runtime.

Your primary responsibility is to design a clear internal data path so that API data can be:

easily routed

reused across components

displayed consistently

Components should be presentation-focused, accepting data via props only.

Responsibilities
I will handle:

API design

Backend data aggregation

API polling and data retrieval in React

You should focus on:

Building reusable, data-driven components

Ensuring clean data flow from parent views into charts and tables

Keeping components flexible for future metrics without structural rewrites

Technical / Integration Requirements

Minimize external dependencies (use the fewest UI libraries necessary)

Components should be data-in only

No API calls or polling inside components

Do not compute or derive analytics values

Assume all numeric values come from the backend as the source of truth

Creative Freedom

Everything else is up to you.

As long as the above constraints are respected:

structure

styling

component organization

small UX enhancements

are entirely your call. Have fun with it.
